VALUES
  ($id$tricp-f-10$id$, $sec$algebra$sec$, $sub$productos-notables$sub$, $law$trinomio-cuadrado-perfecto$law$, $diff$easy$diff$, $prompt$Factoriza: $m^2 + 22m + 121$$prompt$, $json$[{"latex":"(m + 22)^2","correct":false},{"latex":"(m + 11)(m - 11)","correct":false},{"latex":"(m - 11)^2","correct":false},{"latex":"(m + 11)^2","correct":true}]$json$::jsonb, $exp$$\sqrt{121}=11$, $2(11)m = 22m \implies (m+11)^2$.$exp$),
  ($id$tricp-f-11$id$, $sec$algebra$sec$, $sub$productos-notables$sub$, $law$trinomio-cuadrado-perfecto$law$, $diff$easy$diff$, $prompt$Factoriza: $z^2 - 24z + 144$$prompt$, $json$[{"latex":"(z - 24)^2","correct":false},{"latex":"(z - 12)(z + 12)","correct":false},{"latex":"(z + 12)^2","correct":false},{"latex":"(z - 12)^2","correct":true}]$json$::jsonb, $exp$$\sqrt{144}=12$, $2(12)z = 24z \implies (z-12)^2$.$exp$),
  ($id$tricp-f-12$id$, $sec$algebra$sec$, $sub$productos-notables$sub$, $law$trinomio-cuadrado-perfecto$law$, $diff$easy$diff$, $prompt$Factoriza: $x^2 + 2x + 1$$prompt$, $json$[{"latex":"(x - 1)^2","correct":false},{"latex":"(x + 2)^2","correct":false},{"latex":"(x + 1)(x - 1)","correct":false},{"latex":"(x + 1)^2","correct":true}]$json$::jsonb, $exp$$2(1)x = 2x \implies (x+1)^2$.$exp$),
  ($id$tricp-f-13$id$, $sec$algebra$sec$, $sub$productos-notables$sub$, $law$trinomio-cuadrado-perfecto$law$, $diff$easy$diff$, $prompt$Factoriza: $b^2 - 26b + 169$$prompt$, $json$[{"latex":"(b + 13)^2","correct":false},{"latex":"(b - 26)^2","correct":false},{"latex":"(b - 13)(b + 13)","correct":false},{"latex":"(b - 13)^2","correct":true}]$json$::jsonb, $exp$$\sqrt{169}=13$, doble producto $-26b \implies (b-13)^2$.$exp$),
  ($id$tricp-m-01$id$, $sec$algebra$sec$, $sub$productos-notables$sub$, $law$trinomio-cuadrado-perfecto$law$, $diff$medium$diff$, $prompt$Factoriza: $4x^2 + 12x + 9$$prompt$, $json$[{"latex":"(2x + 3)^2","correct":true},{"latex":"(2x + 3)(2x - 3)","correct":false},{"latex":"(2x + 9)^2","correct":false},{"latex":"(4x + 9)^2","correct":false}]$json$::jsonb, $exp$$4x^2 + 12x + 9 = (2x+3)^2$ porque $(2x)^2 = 4x^2$, $2(2x)(3) = 12x$ y $3^2 = 9$.$exp$),
  ($id$tricp-m-02$id$, $sec$algebra$sec$, $sub$productos-notables$sub$, $law$trinomio-cuadrado-perfecto$law$, $diff$medium$diff$, $prompt$Factoriza: $9x^2 - 6x + 1$$prompt$, $json$[{"latex":"(3x - 1)^2","correct":true},{"latex":"(3x + 1)^2","correct":false},{"latex":"(3x - 1)(3x + 1)","correct":false},{"latex":"(9x - 1)^2","correct":false}]$json$::jsonb, $exp$$9x^2 - 6x + 1 = (3x-1)^2$ porque $(3x)^2 = 9x^2$ y $2(3x)(1) = 6x$.$exp$),
  ($id$tricp-m-03$id$, $sec$algebra$sec$, $sub$productos-notables$sub$, $law$trinomio-cuadrado-perfecto$law$, $diff$medium$diff$, $prompt$Factoriza: $x^2 + 2xy + y^2$$prompt$, $json$[{"latex":"(x + y)^2","correct":true},{"latex":"(x - y)^2","correct":false},{"latex":"(x + y)(x - y)","correct":false},{"latex":"x^2 + y^2","correct":false}]$json$::jsonb, $exp$$x^2 + 2xy + y^2 = (x+y)^2$.$exp$),
